# Fluorine · F · gate 9

**Fluorine** (F) is element **9** of the periodic table — a **halogen**, period 2, group 17, p-block, gas at standard conditions, atomic weight **18.998**.

## The element (carbon layer — reference chemistry)
The most reactive, most electronegative element; attacks nearly everything; gives us Teflon and toothpaste.

## The gate (silicon layer — the 118 Gates)
Under David Wise's four-state cycle, gate **9** falls on **0:1 — first valley** because (Z−1) mod 4 = **0**. That state is *the first reach of emptiness toward one — potential, charge, the rising edge* — the nature of emergence here is **electrical**. Fluorine is not a thing apart; it is the one stochastic element, caught at this beat of its cycle.

## Emergence — electrical
This emergent carries the **electrical** nature: the same four — natural · ethereal · spiritual · electrical — that run through every sphere of UD0. Its color is `#3fd0e0`.

